Z||000014||rogergarrison||02-04-2001||10:35 AM||||that clear stuff by 3M is really great stuff. Its not supposed to yellow ever. It makes great door edge protector too, you cant see it and it is tough. Its the same as they put on the front of rear wheels on vans and pickups. I used it on my bumpers so a minor bump or stones wouldnt chip it. One problem is it only works on flat areas, doesnt do too good on compound curves. Using a hair drier might help. Also when you put it on a larger area, use water with a few drops of dish soap and a plastic squeege like putting on window tint. If you try dry it will bubble, so strong if you try to pull it up and redo it will pull your paint off. It fit on my car because the bumpers and nose of mine are flat, its a Ferrari rebody.<P>Bras and car covers DO breath, but the fabric inside stays damp for a long time. If you paint, dont even think of putting a bra or cover over it for a few months. The paint has to cure first.<p>[This message has been edited by rogergarrison (edited 02-04-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000015||firstfiero||02-04-2001||06:31 PM||||      I leave it on all the time...I have a big patch on my hood and the paints already bad their so I don't care. If your paints good the car looks better without one anyway. my 2 cents||||reg||1
Z||000016||Fformula88||02-04-2001||09:52 PM||||My fathers new 85 SE has a LeBra on the front (probably nearly identical to fierojunky's.  It covers just the front Fascia and doesn't impede on the hood at all.  The paint is in decent shape underneath.  Were not going to keep it on full time.  <P>------------------<BR>John<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/formula2m6/FIEROSIG1.JPG">      <BR>1988 Fiero Formula<BR>1985 Fiero SE 2m6<BR>1987 Fiero Sport Coupe *In rebuilding*<BR>1997 Ford Probe SE<BR>AOL IM: Fformula88||||reg||1
Z||000017||frontal lobe||02-05-2001||12:11 AM||||I'm with Hugh.  I like the look of the car better without the bra.  When I bought mine, there was one on it and the first thing I did was take it off.<P>Also, as with Hugh, it is completely a personal taste choice and in no way am I critical of people who like the look.  I was always interested in how many preferred the bras vs. not.||||reg||1
Z||000018||Monkeyman||02-05-2001||12:30 AM||||I guess I haven't seen too many Fieros with bras, 'cause I didn't even remember that there were two styles.  I like the look of a bra, personally.  Since I don't open the hood very often (and the paint isn't the best feature of the car), I'll probably get one of the over-the-hood versions sometime soon.  I <I>will</I> remove my GT hood emblem first.  I'd hate for that to get damaged although I plan on filling in the holes before I paint it.||||reg||1
